ud6.4:1.3:
But there were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The world is not eternal — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." There were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The world is finite — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." But there were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The world is infinite — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." There were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "That which is soul, that is
the body — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." But there were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The soul is one thing, the body is another thing, — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." There were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The individual exists after death — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." But there were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The individual does not exist after death — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." There were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The individual exists and does not exist after death — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." But there were some ascetics and brāhmaṇas who were of this argument, this view: "The individual neither exists nor does not exist after death — this alone is the truth,
else is foolish." They lived contending, quarelling, disputing, attacking each other with sharp tongues,
: "Such is Dhamma, such is not Dhamma; such is not Dhamma, such is Dhamma."
